// TAG-149 example-12.9: mutex completeness on OR's group sources.
//
// The source `{A0<> A1<>}` is a mutex: at most one member is valid
// at a time. Same for `{B0<> B1<>}`. Each row picks one member from
// each group (the other is `null`) and checks the OR response: the
// four valid combinations map to ms_0=0 or ms_1=1 per the row table.
//
// Each row runs in its own Environment (fresh Testbench per row in
// runVectors), so no reset rows are needed between them.
@dut(OR149)
@vectors(A0,A1,B0,B1 : 0,1)

0,null,0,null    : 0,-
0,null,null,1    : -,1
null,1,0,null    : -,1
null,1,null,1    : -,1